	(text_box "The main changes between Professional DOS 1.02 and Disk Demon are as follows:\n\n1) EPROM changed from 27128 to 27256.\nThe main reason for the change in size appears to be because the Disk Demon ROM contains a complete copy of the original Commodore 1541 DOS.\nThis ROM is selected by the @D0 command from the Commodore 64\n\n2)The circuitry for the 2Mhz clock generator has been simplified. A14 & A1 are no longer used to enable it\nU6A is now used to switch between CBM 1541 DOS and Disk Demon DOS.\nU6B is used to enable 2Mhz\n\n3) The values of R1, R2, R3 & R4 are different, slightly shortening the pulse duration generated by U2\n\nRev 2 Additional modifications\nThe original R1 & R2 have been replaced by a single 10k resistor (R1)\nThe original R3 & R4 have been replaced by a single 10k resistor (R2)\nU1, 82S123 PROM has been replaced with an ATF16V8 PLD\n\nRev 3 - Additional modifications\nU3 moved & pins renumbered\nU1 moved from under the CPU to simplify access and assembly\nDiodes D1 & D2 moved from edge of PCB\nAdded bypass Capacitors C4, C5 & C6, 100nF\nUnused inputs for U3C & U3B no longer open circuit\n\nRev 4\nCorrected error in Schematic\nU6, Pin 1 & Pin 13 now connect to RES/		\nU6, Pin 4 & Pin 10 now connect to R7 (1K)\nAdded bypass Capacitor C7, 100nF	\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 293.37 168.91 0)
		(size 104.14 65.2872)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f48d45fe-5698-48b9-9835-2ca57b79e715")
	)
